<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Academia Imperial de Belas Artes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Academia Imperial de Belas Artes was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-academy">Imperial Academy</a> of Fine Arts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a>, the main official art institution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>. It grew out of a group of French artists invited to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in the early nineteenth century and trained generations of Brazilian painters, sculptors and architects. It promoted academic and national <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theme-system">themes</a> in art under imperial patronage.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/academia-imperial-de-belas-artes.jpg" alt="Academia Imperial de Belas Artes" width="316" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Núcleo de digitalização / IMS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Escola_Nacional_de_Belas_Artes_-_8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
